01:14:09,640 --> 01:14:10,720
Right here.

2469
01:14:10,780 --> 01:14:12,460
(The same material)

2470
01:14:17,800 --> 01:14:18,960
Before I changed clothes,

2471
01:14:19,480 --> 01:14:20,760
(Good catch)
I'd already spotted it.

2472
01:14:20,760 --> 01:14:22,000
So I stayed away.

2473
01:14:22,000 --> 01:14:23,240
Let's check his arm

2474
01:14:23,240 --> 01:14:24,400
for any marks.

2475
01:14:24,880 --> 01:14:26,040
Let's take a look.

2476
01:14:26,040 --> 01:14:26,600
Check over there.

2477
01:14:26,600 --> 01:14:28,060
(She saw thread matching her costume)

2478
01:14:28,060 --> 01:14:29,100
(So she didn't approach the evidence)

2479
01:14:32,080 --> 01:14:33,010
Holy moly.

2480
01:14:35,000 --> 01:14:36,480
Still searching?

2481
01:14:36,960 --> 01:14:38,280
Still want to search next time?

2482
01:14:40,480 --> 01:14:41,400
Everything was on my side.

2483
01:14:41,400 --> 01:14:42,080
All the odds favoured me.

2484
01:14:42,080 --> 01:14:43,140
(Humblebrag)
I almost feel bad.

2485
01:14:43,480 --> 01:14:44,080
How did we miss that?

2486
01:14:44,140 --> 01:14:45,460
(They missed the key evidence again)

2487
01:14:46,440 --> 01:14:47,080
You played really well.

2488
01:14:47,480 --> 01:14:48,240
Well played.

2489
01:14:48,240 --> 01:14:49,240
I never once

2490
01:14:49,240 --> 01:14:50,680
suspected you.

2491
01:14:50,840 --> 01:14:53,840
Still, you escaped without a vote.

2492
01:14:54,160 --> 01:14:55,200
Not one vote went to you.

2493
01:14:55,200 --> 01:14:56,300
(I never suspected you)

2494
01:14:56,520 --> 01:14:57,360
Can I ask something?

2495
01:14:57,360 --> 01:14:59,180
Do I get three golden keys
for escaping with zero votes?

2496
01:14:59,180 --> 01:15:00,220
(Seizing the chance for more keys)

2497
01:15:00,680 --> 01:15:01,800
Probably not. Right.

2498
01:15:03,520 --> 01:15:04,120
Let me tell you.

2499
01:15:04,120 --> 01:15:06,040
Happiness lies in contentment.

2500
01:15:06,060 --> 01:15:07,360
(He's motto:
Happiness lies in contentment)

2501
01:15:07,360 --> 01:15:09,920
All right, thank you, everyone.

2502
01:15:17,440 --> 01:15:17,880
What's wrong?

2503
01:15:21,280 --> 01:15:22,160
Quick, lock her in.

2504
01:15:23,000 --> 01:15:23,760
Don't lock me up.

2505
01:15:23,760 --> 01:15:24,720
I'm the killer. Don't lock me up.

2506
01:15:27,680 --> 01:15:27,960
What...

2507
01:15:27,960 --> 01:15:28,520
What is this?

2508
01:15:29,440 --> 01:15:30,320
Players,

2509
01:15:30,320 --> 01:15:32,480
the Door of Truth transfer system
has encountered a bug.

2510
01:15:33,120 --> 01:15:34,720
I'm the designer of the Door of Truth.

2511
01:15:34,720 --> 01:15:35,840
(Door of Truth designer: Designer Bai
Played by Bai Qichen)

2512
01:15:35,840 --> 01:15:36,280
Designer Bai?

2513
01:15:36,280 --> 01:15:37,320
I'm now granting access

2514
01:15:37,320 --> 01:15:39,280
for players to rate the dungeon.

2515
01:15:39,280 --> 01:15:40,040
Rate it?

2516
01:15:40,040 --> 01:15:41,640
We're rating it inside the dungeon?

2517
01:15:41,700 --> 01:15:42,760
(For the first two dungeon ratings,
see Dungeon Archived)

2518
01:15:42,760 --> 01:15:44,040
Congrats on clearing the dungeon.

2519
01:15:44,560 --> 01:15:45,880
Please use the scorecard

2520
01:15:45,880 --> 01:15:48,080
to rate this chapter of your lives.

2521
01:15:48,080 --> 01:15:49,480
Use the scorecard

2522
01:15:49,480 --> 01:15:51,840
to rate the Starlight Cafe dungeon.

2523
01:15:53,280 --> 01:15:54,280
It was incredible.

2524
01:15:54,920 --> 01:15:56,160
It's right here.

2525
01:15:56,600 --> 01:15:57,200
Come on.

2526
01:15:57,200 --> 01:15:57,560
Alright.

2527
01:16:00,960 --> 01:16:02,400
In this Dungeon World,

2528
01:16:02,400 --> 01:16:03,800
whether you were heroes or generals,

2529
01:16:03,800 --> 01:16:05,120
or princes and princesses of each realm,

2530
01:16:05,560 --> 01:16:07,800
you all wished to help the world.

2531
01:16:08,040 --> 01:16:10,560
You rode and fought side by side.

2532
01:16:10,560 --> 01:16:12,240
You kept children safe from harm

2533
01:16:12,240 --> 01:16:14,600
and gave the elderly peace.

2534
01:16:14,600 --> 01:16:15,520
Through your efforts,

2535
01:16:15,520 --> 01:16:17,040
the realm was safe and at peace.

2536
01:16:17,040 --> 01:16:18,640
Your loved ones were by your side.

2537
01:16:18,640 --> 01:16:20,480
Love and hate were resolved.
You lived without regret.

2538
01:16:20,480 --> 01:16:21,280
In future generations' eyes,

2539
01:16:21,280 --> 01:16:22,280
every one of you

2540
01:16:22,280 --> 01:16:23,720
became heroes
whose legends would live on.

2541
01:16:23,720 --> 01:16:24,640
Do you

2542
01:16:24,640 --> 01:16:26,720
like such a meaningful
and beautiful world?

2543
01:16:26,960 --> 01:16:28,400
This is complete nonsense.

2544
01:16:29,760 --> 01:16:30,640
Keep...

2545
01:16:30,640 --> 01:16:31,520
children safe from harm?

2546
01:16:32,040 --> 01:16:33,670
We only wanted to protect them.

2547
01:16:34,000 --> 01:16:36,800
But the children suffered a lot.

2548
01:16:36,800 --> 01:16:37,560
Exactly.

2549
01:16:37,560 --> 01:16:39,280
The elderly were displaced too.

2550
01:16:39,440 --> 01:16:40,960
And the realm wasn't safe

2551
01:16:40,960 --> 01:16:42,000
or at peace.

2552
01:16:42,000 --> 01:16:42,320
Right.

2553
01:16:42,320 --> 01:16:42,920
Exactly.

2554
01:16:42,920 --> 01:16:45,240
And our loved ones weren't with us.

2555
01:16:45,240 --> 01:16:46,000
Exactly.

2556
01:16:46,000 --> 01:16:47,280
Our friends and family all...

2557
01:16:47,280 --> 01:16:48,440
We all ended up homeless.

2558
01:16:48,440 --> 01:16:50,120
Our parents all died.

2559
01:16:50,120 --> 01:16:50,720
Right.

2560
01:16:50,720 --> 01:16:52,600
Those were the things we wanted.

2561
01:16:52,600 --> 01:16:54,760
No, that's how the game described it.

2562
01:16:54,760 --> 01:16:55,680
But what actually happened

2563
01:16:55,680 --> 01:16:58,120
was nothing like that.

2564
01:16:58,280 --> 01:17:00,760
This life story is the exact opposite

2565
01:17:00,760 --> 01:17:02,800
of everything I experienced.

2566
01:17:02,800 --> 01:17:04,640
Do you like

2567
01:17:04,640 --> 01:17:06,880
such a meaningful and beautiful life?

2568
01:17:06,880 --> 01:17:07,680
What?

2569
01:17:08,000 --> 01:17:09,520
Of course that's wrong.

2570
01:17:10,680 --> 01:17:12,120
It's completely different

2571
01:17:12,120 --> 01:17:14,440
from the story we lived through.

2572
01:17:14,500 --> 01:17:18,740
(Why is the dungeon description
so different from their experience?)

2573
01:17:18,760 --> 01:17:20,440
The maximum score is 100.

2574
01:17:20,440 --> 01:17:23,080
Let's give Designer Bai...

2575
01:17:24,440 --> 01:17:25,480
minus 100. How about that?

2576
01:17:25,500 --> 01:17:27,180
(The game doesn't match reality,
so they give it a low score)

2577
01:17:27,180 --> 01:17:28,260
(The game detected an anomaly.
For everyone's safety,)

2578
01:17:28,260 --> 01:17:28,880
(please give a high score.)

2579
01:17:28,880 --> 01:17:30,680
The game detected an anomaly.

2580
01:17:30,680 --> 01:17:32,200
For everyone's safety,

2581
01:17:32,200 --> 01:17:33,960
please give a high score.

2582
01:17:35,320 --> 01:17:36,200
Give it 100 points.

2583
01:17:36,790 --> 01:17:38,380
(Survival instincts maxed out)
A hundred.

2584
01:17:39,080 --> 01:17:40,920
Why is it threatening us?

2585
01:17:41,520 --> 01:17:41,960
No.

2586
01:17:42,560 --> 01:17:44,840
What if I refuse?

2587
01:17:44,840 --> 01:17:46,320
Who are you?

2588
01:17:46,320 --> 01:17:48,120
Zero points.

2589
01:17:48,840 --> 01:17:51,360
Why should I do what it says?

2590
01:17:51,360 --> 01:17:52,800
Though I already wrote 99.

2591
01:17:53,720 --> 01:17:55,120
I gave it 100.

2592
01:17:55,120 --> 01:17:56,280
Let me out. I want to go home.

2593
01:17:56,300 --> 01:17:57,620
(As expected of the detective duo)

2594
01:17:57,800 --> 01:17:58,960
I don't bow to pressure.

2595
01:17:59,520 --> 01:18:00,840
Zero points.

2596
01:18:04,000 --> 01:18:05,480
Bro...

2597
01:18:05,480 --> 01:18:06,600
We got crushed.

2598
01:18:07,080 --> 01:18:08,160
He's panicking.

2599
01:18:08,160 --> 01:18:09,040
He's lost it.

2600
01:18:09,040 --> 01:18:09,960
Who gave it

2601
01:18:09,960 --> 01:18:11,280
999 points?

2602
01:18:11,720 --> 01:18:12,120
Who wrote nine...

2603
01:18:12,120 --> 01:18:12,520
Me.

2604
01:18:14,520 --> 01:18:15,240
He wrote

2605
01:18:15,240 --> 01:18:17,480
9.9.

2606
01:18:17,500 --> 01:18:18,700
(How is that different from 100?)

2607
01:18:18,700 --> 01:18:19,740
(The game detected an anomaly.
For everyone's safety,)

2608
01:18:19,740 --> 01:18:20,300
(please give a high score.)

2609
01:18:20,300 --> 01:18:22,980
(Give it a low score!)

2610
01:18:23,640 --> 01:18:25,120
(Give it a low score!)
Someone says to score it low.

2611
01:18:25,120 --> 01:18:25,960
Give it a low score!

2612
01:18:26,200 --> 01:18:27,400
A low score? Okay.

2613
01:18:27,720 --> 01:18:28,520
We'll give it a low score.

2614
01:18:29,020 --> 01:18:30,420
(What kind of move is this?)

2615
01:18:30,840 --> 01:18:31,440
How did this...

2616
01:18:31,440 --> 01:18:32,120
I already scored it.

2617
01:18:32,400 --> 01:18:33,360
You gave it a high score.

2618
01:18:34,000 --> 01:18:34,840
Change it. Hurry.

2619
01:18:35,400 --> 01:18:36,920
Who gave it 99?

2620
01:18:37,720 --> 01:18:38,640
That was me.

2621
01:18:38,640 --> 01:18:41,240
There was no chivalry at all.

2622
01:18:41,240 --> 01:18:41,680
We...

2623
01:18:41,680 --> 01:18:43,080
We must stand firm.

2624
01:18:44,160 --> 01:18:45,440
Hurry and give it a low score.

2625
01:18:45,440 --> 01:18:45,720
Here.

2626
01:18:45,720 --> 01:18:46,560
Hurry and score it low.

2627
01:18:46,560 --> 01:18:47,800
Change it to a low score.

2628
01:18:47,800 --> 01:18:48,800
It's an obedience test.

2629
01:18:48,800 --> 01:18:50,200
We just do whatever we're told.

2630
01:18:51,000 --> 01:18:52,720
Someone is threatening us,

2631
01:18:52,720 --> 01:18:54,160
saying we must give a high score.

2632
01:18:54,160 --> 01:18:55,520
(Two opposing forces?)
Accept the threat,

2633
01:18:55,520 --> 01:18:56,240
(One wants high, one wants low)
and give a high score.

2634
01:18:56,800 --> 01:18:57,560
But if you think,

2635
01:18:57,560 --> 01:18:59,320
I refuse to play by their rules,

2636
01:18:59,320 --> 01:19:00,400
then give it a low score.

2637
01:19:00,400 --> 01:19:01,840
They want us to defy them.

2638
01:19:01,840 --> 01:19:02,640
Maybe the bad guy

2639
01:19:02,640 --> 01:19:03,720
wants us to score it high.

2640
01:19:04,240 --> 01:19:05,080
Right.

2641
01:19:05,080 --> 01:19:06,040
But actually,

2642
01:19:06,040 --> 01:19:06,680
he threatened us.

2643
01:19:06,680 --> 01:19:07,120
He threatened us.

2644
01:19:07,120 --> 01:19:08,320
Good people don't threaten others.

2645
01:19:08,320 --> 01:19:08,600
Right.

2646
01:19:08,600 --> 01:19:11,540
(Who told the players
to give a low score?)

2647
01:19:11,540 --> 01:19:12,180
(System error)

2648
01:19:12,300 --> 01:19:13,600
(System restored)

2649
01:19:13,600 --> 01:19:14,640
System restored.

2650
01:19:15,280 --> 01:19:16,760
The third game dungeon,

2651
01:19:16,760 --> 01:19:18,520
Ghost Stories of Tui City, is rated.

2652
01:19:18,760 --> 01:19:20,000
Now calculating the golden keys

2653
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:22,120
earned from the third dungeon.

2654
01:19:22,180 --> 01:19:23,420
None.

2655
01:19:23,430 --> 01:19:24,340
(Dungeon 3: Zero golden keys)
Not a single one.

2656
01:19:24,620 --> 01:19:25,740
(Golden Key Leaderboard)

2657
01:19:25,740 --> 01:19:27,060
(Liu Yuning: 5. Jin Jing, Zhang Linghe,
Ding Chengxin, Zhou Keyu: 3)

2658
01:19:27,060 --> 01:19:27,940
(Yang Chaoyue, Wang Yuwen, Sun Qian: 1)

2659
01:19:29,240 --> 01:19:30,040
Golden keys.

2660
01:19:30,800 --> 01:19:31,920
Golden keys, here I come!

2661
01:19:31,920 --> 01:19:32,520
How do we open it?

2662
01:19:34,240 --> 01:19:35,520
We can't even open this.

2663
01:19:35,520 --> 01:19:36,720
No wonder I'm the dumbest one.

2664
01:19:37,200 --> 01:19:38,760
Could it be a drawer?

2665
01:19:39,000 --> 01:19:40,000
Is it this side?

2666
01:19:40,000 --> 01:19:40,480
Not this side.

2667
01:19:41,880 --> 01:19:42,600
How about

2668
01:19:42,600 --> 01:19:44,160
we share the key?

2669
01:19:44,560 --> 01:19:45,600
(Keeping the peace)
Exactly.

2670
01:19:46,080 --> 01:19:47,480
An anomaly was detected
in Dungeon 3.

2671
01:19:47,480 --> 01:19:49,160
Skill card delivery failed.

2672
01:19:49,160 --> 01:19:52,240
To protect the players,

2673
01:19:52,240 --> 01:19:54,000
you will now be transported

2674
01:19:54,000 --> 01:19:56,200
to Dungeon 4.

2675
01:19:57,680 --> 01:19:59,840
No! I haven't got my golden keys!

2676
01:19:59,840 --> 01:20:00,440
(Hahaha)

2677
01:20:00,440 --> 01:20:01,360
No!

2678
01:20:02,120 --> 01:20:03,800
(Opening the transport portal)
Give me my golden keys!

2679
01:20:03,920 --> 01:20:04,480
No!

2680
01:20:04,920 --> 01:20:06,040
My golden keys!

2681
01:20:06,040 --> 01:20:07,520
Two keys.

2682
01:20:07,520 --> 01:20:09,200
I have two golden keys!

2683
01:20:09,600 --> 01:20:11,920
Stop laughing! Help me open it!

2684
01:20:12,720 --> 01:20:15,000
I'm begging you!

2685
01:20:15,000 --> 01:20:16,520
To keep it fair,

2686
01:20:16,520 --> 01:20:17,440
how about none of us takes it?

2687
01:20:17,440 --> 01:20:17,920
No one gets it.

2688
01:20:18,760 --> 01:20:20,080
No, guys!

2689
01:20:20,080 --> 01:20:20,720
Why?

2690
01:20:21,320 --> 01:20:22,560
We won't take ours either.

2691
01:20:22,560 --> 01:20:23,800
Then nobody gains any points.

2692
01:20:23,800 --> 01:20:24,040
No one does.

2693
01:20:24,040 --> 01:20:24,960
So if you have zero,

2694
01:20:24,960 --> 01:20:25,400
you'll stay at zero.

2695
01:20:25,400 --> 01:20:26,200
And we'll still...

2696
01:20:27,600 --> 01:20:28,800
You'll regret this.

2697
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:31,600
From this day forward,

2698
01:20:31,600 --> 01:20:33,240
in every dungeon to come,

2699
01:20:33,240 --> 01:20:36,320
I won't just kill those named Tui.

2700
01:20:36,600 --> 01:20:38,360
I'll kill all of you too!

2701
01:20:39,800 --> 01:20:42,400
Welcome aboard
the Tongcheng Travel Time Tunnel

2702
01:20:42,400 --> 01:20:43,600
to the dungeon world.

2703
01:20:44,080 --> 01:20:45,600
I'll be your guide,

2704
01:20:45,600 --> 01:20:47,400
Fei Ermeng from Tongcheng Travel.

2705
01:20:47,760 --> 01:20:50,480
Please collect your personal
dungeon passes.

2706
01:20:50,480 --> 01:20:51,720
Change outfits and transform.

2707
01:20:51,720 --> 01:20:52,680
Get ready to depart.

2708
01:20:53,120 --> 01:20:55,440
Investigate with ease.
I'll be with you throughout.

2709
01:20:55,440 --> 01:20:57,080
Let's set off with Tongcheng.

2710
01:21:06,540 --> 01:21:08,020
(Player Liu Yuning obtained identity:
Ning Watcha)

2711
01:21:11,500 --> 01:21:13,220
(Player Jin Jing obtained identity:
Jin Goofy)

2712
01:21:15,900 --> 01:21:17,060
(Player Zhang Linghe obtained identity:
He Struggle)

2713
01:21:19,060 --> 01:21:21,340
(Player Ding Chengxin obtained identity:
Ding Staring)

2714
01:21:23,580 --> 01:21:25,500
(Player Zhou Keyu obtained identity:
Ke Uh-Oh)

2715
01:21:27,220 --> 01:21:29,460
(Guest Player Zhang Ruonan identity:
Nan Shy)

2716
01:21:29,460 --> 01:21:32,020
(Case 4 loading...)

2717
01:21:50,340 --> 01:21:52,060
(After completing this story,
what are your thoughts and reflections?)

2718
01:21:52,080 --> 01:21:53,080
In this story,

2719
01:21:53,080 --> 01:21:54,360
the character I played, Hehe,

2720
01:21:54,360 --> 01:21:55,560
donated the treasure

2721
01:21:55,560 --> 01:21:56,600
from his ancestral hometown

2722
01:21:56,600 --> 01:21:57,880
with a very simple intention.

2723
01:21:57,880 --> 01:21:58,600
He hoped that this piece of history,

2724
01:21:58,600 --> 01:22:00,840
filled with courage
and valuable lessons,

2725
01:22:00,840 --> 01:22:02,360
could be seen by more people.

2726
01:22:02,480 --> 01:22:04,200
But someone took advantage
of that trust,

2727
01:22:04,200 --> 01:22:06,120
(Zuixian Inn)
turning something of public value

2728
01:22:06,120 --> 01:22:07,960
into a tool for personal gain.

2729
01:22:07,960 --> 01:22:08,800
No one should monopolize it

2730
01:22:08,800 --> 01:22:10,840
for their own selfish interests,

2731
01:22:10,840 --> 01:22:12,760
let alone profit from it.

2732
01:22:12,760 --> 01:22:14,360
That is a desecration of history.

2733
01:22:14,440 --> 01:22:15,920
I once desperately

2734
01:22:15,920 --> 01:22:17,680
wanted to hide away every treasure.

2735
01:22:17,680 --> 01:22:18,200
Later,

2736
01:22:18,200 --> 01:22:18,840
I finally understood

2737
01:22:18,840 --> 01:22:21,760
that true protection
is not about possession,

2738
01:22:21,760 --> 01:22:23,600
but making sure it never falls

2739
01:22:23,680 --> 01:22:24,560
into the hands of those
with evil intentions.

2740
01:22:24,560 --> 01:22:26,080
As long as there are people
willing to step forward

2741
01:22:26,080 --> 01:22:29,080
and protect these relics
that carry our history,

2742
01:22:29,080 --> 01:22:31,320
our roots will never be erased.

2743
01:22:31,320 --> 01:22:33,280
In this case,
much of the advanced technology

2744
01:22:33,280 --> 01:22:34,960
was only used for profit.

2745
01:22:34,960 --> 01:22:36,400
I believe we must reject

2746
01:22:36,400 --> 01:22:38,280
